It is my lunch break at work.
I call a local clinic.
I would like to book an appointment with the dentist.
A receptionist answers the phone.
"Can you come on Thursday?" he asks.
"We have an appointment at quarter past two."
I look at the calendar on my phone.
Thursday afternoon suits me fine.
"Yes, quarter past two is perfect," I say.
"Great, what is your phone number?" he asks.
"My number is 12 34 56 78," I answer.
He confirms my appointment, and I hang up.
Now I am ready to work again.
